==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|es|Venezuela}}, from {{der|en|it|Veneziola}}, diminutive of {{m|it|Venezia|t=[[Venice]]}}, after the stilt houses reminiscent of Venetian architecture.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌvɛn.ɪˈzweɪ.lə/|/ˌvɛn.ɛzˈweɪ.lə/|/ˌvɛn.əˈzweɪ.lə/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Soundguys-Venezuela.wav|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Venezuela.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪlə|s=4}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# {{senseid|en|Q717}}{{place|en|country|cont/South America|caplc=Caracas|official=Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Clare Foran, Haley Talbot and Priscilla Alvarez|title=Congress passes immigrant detention bill in first legislative win for Trump|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/22/politics/laken-riley-act-house-immigrant-detention-vote/index.html|date=2025-01-22|passage=The legislation is named after Laken Riley, a 22-year old Georgia student who was killed last year while out for a run. An undocumented migrant from '''Venezuela''' was convicted and sentenced to life without parole in the case that reignited a national debate over immigration and crime.}}

